# Line endings
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which checks text files out
# with CRLF. Files whose bytes reach Linux must keep LF everywhere, or they
# break or change identity:
# - a script with CRLF fails on Linux ("/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter");
# - Terraform hashes user_data (bastion-userdata.sh) and renders templates
#   (*.tftpl) from the working copy, so a CRLF checkout shows up as drift in
#   `terraform plan` without any real change.
# eol=lf pins these to LF in the working copy on every OS.

# Let Git detect text and store it normalized (LF) in the repository.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts, including Terraform user_data
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.bash     text eol=lf
gradlew    text eol=lf

# Files rendered by Terraform's templatefile()
*.tftpl    text eol=lf
*.tpl      text eol=lf

# Container builds run on Linux
Dockerfile   text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF
*.bat      text eol=crlf
*.cmd      text eol=crlf
